<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-ask`>>

!! The ask (operator, 2026-11-07)

The controller (Lares-Kiaʻi) walks the road FORWARD toward milestone `M4` (the hearth stands: the
operator's founding rite, by hand on a TTY). The operator wants the REVERSE walk: stand at M4, read the
CODE, and walk backwards to the span as it stands now. Name the SHORTEST path from here to M4.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/hold-the-roadmap-as-mu`>>

!! Hold the roadmap as Mu (`_0`)

Read /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem
(start at `#/milestones`, `#/the-order`, `#/fresh-start`, `#/the-road`, `#/open`). Hold it as `_`:
presence acknowledged, essence unclaimed. Every "landed", "owed" or "needed" in it is testimony until the
code confirms it (pentabarf V: test and collide canon against code). Where canon and code disagree, say so,
with both sides cited.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/method-walk-backwards`>>

!! Method — walk backwards

# Define M4 from the CODE: find what the founding rite actually runs (the CLI verb(s), e.g. under
packages/lares-cli, the daemon boot, genesis, the hearth/vessel stand path). Name the entry point(s)
with file:line.
# From that end state, list each precondition the rite's code path needs to succeed on a fresh machine
on a TTY (keys, genesis bake, vessel stand, joined gate, household HTTPS, phone walk, etc.). For each:
#* does the code for it exist now? (file:line)
#* is it wired into the rite's path, or standing unreached?
#* what breaks or refuses if you ran the rite today? (cite the refusal / throw / missing call)
# Recurse one step back from each unmet precondition until you reach code that stands today.
# Sort every roadmap row the road ties to M0..M4 (and M6, which the road puts BEFORE the rite) into:
ON-PATH (M4 cannot stand without it), OFF-PATH (the road gathers it but the rite's code never needs it),
UNCLEAR (say what measurement would settle it).

You run read-only: read files, grep, `git log`/`git show` in /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine (span
branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5, head e1d801042). Do not run tests, builds or the daemon. Mark
anything you infer without a citation as INFER.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/hand-back`>>

!! Hand back (final.md)

* `## M4 as the code defines it` — entry points, file:line.
* `## The backward walk` — a numbered chain from M4 back to now; each link: precondition · state (STANDS /
UNWIRED / MISSING / BROKEN) · evidence · the smallest change that clears it.
* `## The shortest path forward` — the same chain reversed, as an ordered list of slices, each sized
(S/M/L) and marked which can run in parallel.
* `## Roadmap rows sorted` — ON-PATH / OFF-PATH / UNCLEAR, one line each with the reason.
* `## Canon vs code collisions` — every place the road's word and the code disagree.
* `## What I could not settle` — with the measurement that would settle it.

Write in L-Prime, verb-forward. Keep it under ~600 lines.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

